WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.960
Who actually needs a
Companies House personal code,

2
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.580
and why does it matter so much?

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.440
I get asked this every single
day, so let me answer it properly.

4
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:13.720
I'm from Tax and
Accounting Hub Limited,

5
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.880
an Authorised Corporate
Service Provider,

6
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:17.960
and this is Director Personal Code.

7
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:19.860
First, what it is.

8
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.460
A personal code is an 11-character
code that Companies House issues to you

9
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.020
once you have verified your identity.

10
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.640
It belongs to you,
not to your company.

11
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.240
Think of it as proof,
on the public record,

12
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.380
that Companies House
knows who you really are.

13
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.700
So who needs
one? Four groups.

14
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.430
Company directors, or the equivalent
role in your organisation.

15
00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.820
People with significant control, that
is anyone who owns or controls more

16
00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:45.260
than 25% of the shares
or voting rights.

17
00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.980
Members of a limited
liability partnership.

18
00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:52.440
And anyone who files documents at
Companies House on a company's behalf.

19
00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.100
And a question I hear
constantly from clients abroad.

20
00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:00.640
Does this apply to me if I do not
live in the United Kingdom? Yes.

21
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.060
It is your role that triggers the
requirement, not your address.

22
00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:08.740
If you are a director or a person with
significant control of a UK company,

23
00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:13.680
you must verify, wherever in the
world you happen to live. When?

24
00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.300
Identity verification became a legal
requirement on the 18 November 2025,

25
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.520
and that opened a 12-month
transition period.

26
00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.440
If you were already a director, your
code has to appear on your company's

27
00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.500
next confirmation statement.

28
00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:29.500
If you are appointed, or you
incorporate a new company,

29
00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.440
you need your code at
the point of filing.

30
00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:33.460
Now the important part.

31
00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.000
Why does this matter?

32
00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.770
If you miss your deadline,
you are committing an offence.

33
00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:40.440
Companies House can issue
a financial penalty.

34
00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:43.380
You can be blocked from making
any filings for the company.

35
00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:46.160
And you can be stopped from
starting a new company at all.

36
00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:50.900
This is not a tick box exercise, it has
real consequences for you personally.

37
00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.020
One piece of good news.

38
00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.060
If you sit on several
boards, you only verify once.

39
00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:59.300
The same personal code covers
every appointment you hold,

40
00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:00.880
now and in the future.

41
00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:05.200
And if it is ever compromised, Companies
House will cancel it and issue you

42
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.300
a new one.

43
00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:10.340
As an Authorised Corporate Service
Provider we verify you and file it

44
00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:12.320
directly with Companies
House as your agent,

45
00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.240
online or in person,
wherever you are based.

